    # game/extras.rpy:224
    old "Hello everyone, and thank you for reading {i}{i}My Darling Dark Elf{/i}!{/i} I hope you enjoyed reading it, because I enjoyed writing it! As always, I’ll talk a little about the inspirations behind this story, though I think they might be a bit unexpected in this case hahaha{vspace=30}So! I had the desire to write a story with cute elf girls after I saw a series of anime figures by Vertex. They have a whole line of elf figures called ‘Elf Village’, and I thought some of the designs were pretty cute (though the figure line is quite NSFW). There was one particular figure I really liked of a dark elf called Layla, and I thought her design was so pretty I wanted to design my own cute elf girl with a darker skin tone and purple hair: hence, Nienke was born.{vspace=30}I had the idea for Nienke as a cutesy design before I had an idea for her story. I was toying with the idea of using my elf girl for something, but I didn’t have any particular setting in mind, until I read a couple of books by the Dutch author Johanna van Veen. She writes horror stories set in the Netherlands that are very scenic despite being quite spooky. I liked the general atmosphere of her stories, so I thought, “Hmm, it would be nice to write a story set in the Netherlands too.”{vspace=30}Since I’d already toyed with writing a story about an elf girl, I figured I could just drop my elf girl into a slightly alternate history version of the Netherlands (since there’s an elven/human war mentioned in passing) and call it a day.{vspace=30}I wanted the story to have a bit of a classic vibe, and since I was drawing on the historical setting of van Veen’s {i}My Darling Dreadful Thing{/i} which is set a little after WW2, I figured I’d also go for a more old-fashioned setting without any phones or the internet. I think that makes the story feel most cosy haha.{vspace=30}I didn’t put a definitive date to when {i}My Darling Dark Elf{/i} is set, since I wanted the setting to feel timeless (maybe a little bit like a fairytale), but I presume it’d be in the 1960s or so. I wasn’t really aiming for historical accuracy here though, and I wouldn’t really call this a historical story or a period piece. It’s more of a cosy cottagecore story with cute elf girls.{vspace=30}I think I was also drawing some inspiration from Eva Ibbotson’s stories. She wrote a lot of historical fiction which luxuriates in descriptions of the countryside, the rolling Alps, and the shimmering waters of the Danube, and her writing is so pretty and pleasant to read I always find myself calling back to it when I write more bucolic stuff set in the countryside. If I could have at least some of the skill of Eva Ibbotson then I would be happy!{vspace=30}Initially, I planned for Cornelia, Nienke’s absentee friend, to be the protagonist of this story, while Nienke would be a love interest. The initial iteration of this story was called {i}My Childhood Friend is an Elf{/i} (that’s a very light novel tier title haha), and it was going to be a fairly short, simple romance story between a human and an elf. I wrote a decent chunk of this story (I got about 20,000 words in or so), but I wasn’t too happy with the direction.{vspace=30}I liked the general setting (the earliest version of this story was also set in Alpenrose), and I’d already hashed out a lot of details which carried over into {i}My Darling Dark Elf{/i}, such as Nienke’s parents owning a café that both Nienke and Cornelia work at, and Nienke being teased at school by her classmates, but I felt like the romance wasn’t especially convincing.{vspace=30}I thought Nienke was a more interesting character than Cornelia (and she’s also more to my tastes, since she’s a bit of a tsundere), and I thought the story might work better with her as the lead. My initial vision for this story had in set in school, too, with Cornelia and Nienke being teenagers, but I decided to age them up and send Cornelia away to university.{vspace=30}The original version of the story felt a bit too toothless (well, it was supposed to be light-hearted), and I thought centring the story around the theme of growing older and growing apart from your old friends would make the narrative feel a bit more focused and give it more of a throughline.{vspace=30}Since I decided to banish Cornelia from the narrative (it was her punishment for being a boring protagonist. Sorry, Cornelia), I had to think of a new love interest for Nienke. Since I had already conceptualised her as a character, and I knew I wanted her to be a bit haughty, I decided to give her a love interest who’s more outgoing and a bit of a tomboy to contrast her.{vspace=30}I’m not going to share any of the scenes from the scrapped {i}My Childhood Friend is an Elf{/i} here, since these notes are long enough already, but I do consider a lot of the stuff in that scrapped story to be canon to {i}My Darling Dark Elf{/i}. I used that unreleased story to hash out some details of Nienke and Cornelia’s past, and there’s a bit more information in there about Cornelia’s relationship with her father, Laurens, who only gets mentioned off-handedly in here.{vspace=30}Anyway! That just about sums everything up. This story was inspired by some pretty diverse things, but I hope it all comes together cohesively enough in the end. I’m especially fond of the character art for this story, which is by the very talented Toromi, so it would be nice if you could appreciate that if nothing else!{vspace=30}- ebi x"
    new "大家好，感谢阅读{i}{i}《我亲爱的暗精灵》{/i}！{/i}希望你们读得开心，因为我写的时候很开心！照例，我想聊聊这个故事的灵感来源。不过这次的灵感，可能有些出乎意料，哈哈哈。{vspace=30}那么！最初让我想写可爱精灵女孩的，是 Vertex 的一系列动漫手办。他们有一整个名叫“Elf Village”的精灵手办系列，其中一些设计让我觉得特别可爱——虽然这个系列的尺度相当大。有一款叫蕾拉的暗精灵手办，我尤其喜欢。她的设计太漂亮了，让我也想设计一个深色皮肤、紫色头发的可爱精灵女孩。于是，妮恩克诞生了。{vspace=30}在构思她的故事之前，我先有了妮恩克这个可爱的形象。我一直琢磨着拿这个精灵女孩写点什么，却没有明确的背景设定。直到读了荷兰作家约翰娜·范维恩的几本书，才有了方向。她写的恐怖故事都以荷兰为背景，虽然阴森，却也充满优美的景色。我很喜欢那种整体氛围，心想：“嗯，写个发生在荷兰的故事，应该也不错。”{vspace=30}既然我本来就在考虑写精灵女孩的故事，那干脆把她放进一个历史稍有不同的荷兰就好了。毕竟，文中也顺带提到了精灵与人类之间的战争。{vspace=30}我希望这个故事带点古典气息，又参考了范维恩的{i}《My Darling Dreadful Thing》{/i}所采用的二战结束不久后的历史背景，于是也选择了一个更老派的、没有电话和互联网的时代。我觉得这样更有温馨惬意的感觉，哈哈。{vspace=30}我没有明确设定{i}《我亲爱的暗精灵》{/i}发生在哪一年，因为我想让这个背景有种不受时间限制的感觉，也许有点像童话。不过，我想大概是在二十世纪六十年代左右。当然，我并没有追求历史考据，也不会把它叫作历史故事或年代剧。它更像是一则温馨的田园故事，里面有可爱的精灵女孩。{vspace=30}我想，伊娃·伊博森的作品也给了我一些灵感。她写过很多历史小说，细细描绘乡村、连绵的阿尔卑斯山，以及波光粼粼的多瑙河。她的文字优美，读来又舒适。每当我写乡村背景、田园气息更浓的故事时，总会不自觉地想起她。如果我能有她几分功力，就很满足了！{vspace=30}最初，我打算让妮恩克那位不在身边的朋友科妮莉娅担任主角，妮恩克则是恋爱对象。故事的初版叫{i}《我的青梅竹马是精灵》{/i}——是不是很有轻小说标题的感觉，哈哈。原本，它会是一个篇幅较短、情节简单的人类与精灵相恋的故事。我写了相当一部分，大概两万英文词左右，却对故事的走向不太满意。{vspace=30}我喜欢整体背景，最早的版本也发生在阿尔彭罗瑟。而且，当时已经敲定了不少后来沿用到{i}《我亲爱的暗精灵》{/i}里的细节。比如，妮恩克的父母经营着一家咖啡馆，她和科妮莉娅都在那里帮忙；妮恩克在学校受到同学嘲弄。不过，我觉得那段恋情不太有说服力。{vspace=30}我觉得妮恩克比科妮莉娅更有趣，也更合我的喜好，毕竟她有点傲娇。让她当主角，也许故事会更好。最初的构想还是校园背景，科妮莉娅和妮恩克都只有十几岁，但后来我决定让她们年长一些，再把科妮莉娅送去上大学。{vspace=30}原来的故事感觉少了点力度——虽说，它本来就是走轻松路线的。我想，如果把主题放在逐渐长大、与昔日好友渐行渐远上，叙事就会更集中，也会有一条更明确的主线。{vspace=30}既然决定把科妮莉娅赶出故事——这就是当无趣主角的惩罚。对不起啦，科妮莉娅——我就得给妮恩克想一个新的恋爱对象。我已经构思好了妮恩克，知道自己希望她有点高傲，于是决定给她安排一位更外向、带点假小子气质的恋人，形成对照。{vspace=30}这些后记已经够长了，我就不在这里分享废弃的{i}《我的青梅竹马是精灵》{/i}里的片段了。不过，那个故事中的很多内容，我仍然视作{i}《我亲爱的暗精灵》{/i}的正式设定。那篇未发表的故事帮我理清了妮恩克与科妮莉娅过去的一些细节，也写到了更多科妮莉娅和父亲劳伦斯之间的关系。在这部作品里，他只是被顺口提到了几次。{vspace=30}好啦！大致就是这些。这个故事的灵感来源相当多样，希望最后还是融合得足够自然。我尤其喜欢才华出众的 Toromi 为本作绘制的角色。如果别的方面没能打动你，至少也希望你能喜欢这些画！{vspace=30}—— ebi，亲亲"

